/-- solkey `SolcExpressions.incDecChainOnLocal` (`solc/SolcExpressions.sol`).

solc: expressions/inc_dec_operators.sol — the upstream accumulation
`r = a; r += a++ * 0x10; r += ++a * 0x100` on a local, with each step bound
(0x10 = 16, 0x100 = 256; the expected 6 + 6*16 + 8*256 = 2150).

`T r = x++;` split into `T r; r = x++;`. -/
theorem incDecChainOnLocal :
    Diamond (State.init SolcExpressions)
    sol[SolcExpressions]{
      uint a = 6;
      uint r = a;
      uint p;
      p = a++;
      r = r + p * 16;
      uint q;
      q = ++a;
      r = r + q * 256;
      assert(a == 8);
      assert(r == 2150);
    } := by
  corpus_decide

/-- solkey `SolcExpressions.incDecChainOnStateVariable` (`solc/SolcExpressions.sol`).

solc: expressions/inc_dec_operators.sol — same chain on a state variable
(`v = 3; r += v++ * 0x1000; r += ++v * 0x10000`), so the storage increment rules are
exercised instead of the local ones (0x1000 = 4096, 0x10000 = 65536; the expected
3*4096 + 5*65536 = 339968).

`T r = x++;` split into `T r; r = x++;`. -/
theorem incDecChainOnStateVariable :
    Diamond (State.init SolcExpressions)
    sol[SolcExpressions]{
      counter = 3;
      uint p;
      p = counter++;
      uint r = p * 4096;
      uint q;
      q = ++counter;
      r = r + q * 65536;
      assert(counter == 5);
      assert(r == 339968);
    } := by
  corpus_decide

